        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: harden recovered meeting browser sessions",
        "body": "Related: #109755\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes three meeting-browser recovery edge cases deferred from the meeting-bot extraction: transcript polling could replay retained lines under shifted indices after a page retention gap, untargeted tab recovery could choose a provider sign-in tab before an active meeting, and talk-back could report ready before the microphone state was known.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe transcript store now retains one contiguous tail and preserves its cross-epoch offset whenever the page cursor jumps. Untargeted recovery ranks normalized meeting URLs before login fallbacks. Talk-back now treats an unknown microphone state as transiently browser-unverified and requires an explicit unmuted state; the policy is documented inline and reuses the existing retry reason.\n\nMaintainer decision (July 17, 2026): accept the fail-closed microphone policy. Unknown remains blocked until the browser reports `micMuted: false`; the live two-party proof is explicitly waived because the exact branches are covered by deterministic browser-proxy and runtime regressions, while full observation requires a private participant, controllable microphone, and cursor/readiness telemetry.\n\nThis is AI-assisted maintainer work. I reviewed the implementation, callers, Google Meet and Teams sibling behavior, shipped beta behavior, and the originating history.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMeeting transcript clients no longer receive old lines under new cursor indices after page retention or reload gaps. Browser recovery prefers an actual call even when a sign-in tab appears first. Talk-back waits for verified microphone readiness instead of risking silently dropped speech.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Regression tests failed before the fix for both transcript gap branches, sign-in-first tab enumeration, and unknown microphone readiness.\n- Focused post-fix proof: 10 meeting-bot tests, 7 Google Meet browser transport tests, and 40 Teams sibling tests passed.\n- Exact-diff Blacksmith Testbox changed gate passed: core, core-test, and extension-test typechecks; full core and extension lint; format, SDK, ownership, dependency, import-cycle, and database-first guards.\n- Fresh autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings, patch correct at 0.94 confidence.\n- Live two-party proof waived by the maintainer: exact cursor and readiness observations require a private participant, controllable microphone, and operator-visible poll/readiness telemetry; deterministic regressions exercise those decision boundaries without credentials.\n",
